'\" t
.
.\" ASCII for Unicode ellipsis is three dots
.schar \[u2026] ...
.\" New escape [...] maps to Unicode ellipsis
.char \[...] \[u2026]
.
.\" an-ext.tmac: Check whether we are using grohtml.
.nr mH 0
.if \n(.g \
.  if '\*(.T'html' \
.    nr mH 1
.
.\" What about gropdf?
.nr mP 0
.if \n(.g \
.  if '\*(.T'pdf' \
.    nr mP 1
.
.\" an-ext.tmac: Start example.
.de EX
.  nr mE \\n(.f
.  nf
.  nh
.  ft CW
..
.
.\" an-ext.tmac: End example.
.de EE
.  ft \\n(mE
.  fi
.  hy \\n(HY
..
.
.\" Top level heading; wraps .SH
.de H1
.  if \\n(mP .pdfhref O 1 \\$*
.  SH \\$*
..
.
.\" 2nd level heading; wraps .SS
.de H2
.  if \\n(mP .pdfhref O 2 \\$*
.  SS \\$*
..
.
.\" 3rd level heading; bold font, no indent
.de H3
.  if \\n(.$ \{\
.    if \\n(mP .pdfhref O 3 \\$*
.    .B \&"\\$*"
.  \}
.  br
..
.
.\" Render URL
.de UU
.  ie \\n(mH \{\
\\$1\c
.    do HTML-NS "<a href='\\$2'>"
\\$2\c
.    do HTML-NS "</a>"
\\$3
.  \}
.  el \{\
.    ie \\n(mP \{\
.      pdfhref -W -P "\\$1" -A "\\$3" "\\$2"
.    \}
.    el \{\
\\$1\\$2\\$3
.    \}
.  \}
..
.
.nr PDFOUTLINE.FOLDLEVEL 3
.\"
.pdfview /PageMode /UseOutlines
.pdfinfo /Title xroar @PACKAGE_VERSION@
.pdfinfo /Author Ciaran Anscomb
.
.TH "xroar" "1" "@MANPAGE_DATE@" "xroar-@PACKAGE_VERSION@"
.hy 0
.nh
.H1 NAME
.PP
xroar\[em]Dragon and Tandy 8-bit computer emulator
.H1 SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBxroar\fR \[lB]\f(CB\-c\fR \fIconffile\fR\[rB] \[lB]\fIOPTION\fR\[rB]\[...] \[lB]\fIFILENAME\fR\[rB]\[...]
.H1 DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBXRoar\fR emulates the Dragon 32/64; Tandy Colour Computers 1, 2 and 3; the Tandy MC-10; and some other similar machines or clones. It runs on a wide variety of platforms.
.H1 OPTIONS
.PP
Options are first read from a configuration file (by default, \fI$HOME/.xroar/xroar.conf\fR). Options on the command line override any found in the configuration file.
.TP
\f(CB\-C\fR
Allocate a console window (Windows only).
.TP
\f(CB\-c\fR \fIconffile\fR
Specify a configuration file.
.H2 Machines:
.TP
\f(CB\-m\fR \fIname\fR, \f(CB\-default\-machine\fR \fIname\fR
Default machine profile to select on startup.
.TP
\f(CB\-machine\fR \fIname\fR
Create or modify named machine profile. \f(CB\-machine help\fR lists currently defined profiles.
.PP
The remaining options configure the currently selected machine:
.TP
\f(CB\-machine\-desc\fR \fItext\fR
Machine description shown in \f(CB\-machine help\fR and menu options.
.TP
\f(CB\-machine\-arch\fR \fIarch\fR
Machine architecture (\f(CBdragon64\fR, \f(CBdragon32\fR, \f(CBcoco\fR, \f(CBcoco3\fR or \f(CBmc10\fR).
.TP
\f(CB\-machine\-keyboard\fR \fIlayout\fR
Keyboard layout (\f(CBdragon\fR, \f(CBdragon200e\fR, \f(CBcoco\fR or \f(CBcoco3\fR).
.TP
\f(CB\-machine\-cpu\fR \fIcpu\fR
Machine CPU (\f(CB6809\fR or \f(CB6309\fR). Not applicable to the MC-10.
.TP
\f(CB\-bas\fR \fIrom\fR
ROM image for Colour BASIC (CoCo) or Microcolour BASIC (MC-10).
.TP
\f(CB\-extbas\fR \fIrom\fR
ROM image for Extended BASIC (Super Extended BASIC on the CoCo 3).
.TP
\f(CB\-altbas\fR \fIrom\fR
ROM image for 64K-mode Extended BASIC (Dragon 64, Dragon 200-E).
.TP
\f(CB\-nobas\fR, \f(CB\-noextbas\fR, \f(CB\-noaltbas\fR
Indicate the corresponding ROM is not fitted in this machine.
.TP
\f(CB\-ext\-charset\fR \fIrom\fR
External character generator ROM to use.
.TP
\f(CB\-tv\-type\fR \fItype\fR
TV type (\f(CBpal\fR, \f(CBntsc\fR or \f(CBpal\-m\fR).
.TP
\f(CB\-tv\-input\fR \fIinput\fR
One of \f(CBcmp\fR (composite video, no cross-colour), \f(CBcmp\-br\fR (composite video, blue-red cross-colour), \f(CBcmp\-rb\fR (composite video, red-blue cross-colour) or \f(CBrgb\fR (RGB video, CoCo 3 only).
.TP
\f(CB\-vdg\-type\fR \fItype\fR
Indicate the VDG variant fitted. One of \f(CB6847\fR or \f(CB6847t1\fR.
.TP
\f(CB\-ram\-org\fR \fIorganisation\fR
RAM organisation (\f(CB\-ram\-org help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-ram\fR \fIkbytes\fR
Amount of RAM fitted in kilobytes. Valid sizes are 4–64K for Dragon and Tandy CoCo 1/2; 128K or 512K for the Tandy CoCo 3; 2K, 4K or 20K for the Tandy MC-10.
.TP
\f(CB\-ram\-init\fR \fIpattern\fR
RAM start pattern (\f(CB\-ram\-init help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-machine\-cart\fR \fIname\fR
Default cartridge to attach. \f(CB\-no\-machine\-cart\fR to inhibit the default behaviour of searching for a workign DOS cartridge.
.H2 Cartridges:
.TP
\f(CB\-cart\fR \fIname\fR
Create or modify named cartridge profile. \f(CB\-cart help\fR lists currently defined profiles.
.PP
The remaining options configure the currently selected cartridge:
.TP
\f(CB\-cart\-desc\fR \fItext\fR
Cartridge description shown in \f(CB\-cart help\fR and menu options.
.TP
\f(CB\-cart\-type\fR \fItype\fR
Cartridge base type (\f(CB\-cart\-type help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-cart\-rom\fR \fIrom\fR
ROM image to load ($C000-).
.TP
\f(CB\-cart\-rom2\fR \fIrom\fR
Second ROM image to load ($E000-).
.TP
\f(CB\-cart\-autorun\fR
Autorun cartridge.
.TP
\f(CB\-cart\-becker\fR
Enable becker port where supported.
.TP
\f(CB\-mpi\-slot\fR \fIslot\fR
(MPI) initially select slot (0–3).
.TP
\f(CB\-mpi\-load\-cart\fR \[lB]\fIslot\fR=\[rB]\fIname\fR
(MPI) insert cartridge into next or numbered \fIslot\fR.
.PP
When configuring a Multi-Pak Interface (MPI), only the last configured DOS cartridge will end up connected to the virtual drives. MPI options also apply to the similar RACE Computer Expansion Cage.
.H2 Becker port:
.TP
\f(CB\-becker\fR
Prefer becker-enabled DOS cartridge when picked automatically.
.TP
\f(CB\-becker\-ip\fR \fIaddress\fR
Address or hostname of DriveWire server \[lB]127.0.0.1\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-becker\-port\fR \fIport\fR
Port of DriveWire server \[lB]65504\[rB]
.H2 Cassettes:
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-tape\fR \fIfile\fR
Attach \fIfile\fR as tape image for reading.
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-write\fR \fIfile\fR
Open \fIfile\fR for tape writing.
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-pan\fR \fIpanning\fR
Pan stereo input (0.0 = full left, 1.0 = full right) \[lB]0.5\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-hysteresis\fR \fIpercent\fR
Read hysteresis as percentage of full scale \[lB]1\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-tape\-fast\fR
Disable fast tape loading.
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-tape\-pad\-auto\fR
Disable automatic leader padding.
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-rewrite\fR
Enable tape rewriting.
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-rewrite\-gap\-ms\fR \fIms\fR
Gap length in milliseconds to write in rewrite mode (1–5000ms, default 500ms).
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-rewrite\-leader\fR \fIbytes\fR
Length of leaders in bytes to write in rewrite mode (1–2048 bytes, default 256).
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-ao\-rate\fR \fIhz\fR
Set tape writing frame rate \[lB]9600\[rB]
.H2 Floppy disks:
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-fd\fIX\fB\fR \fIfile\fR
Insert disk image \fIfile\fR into floppy drive \fIX\fR (0–3).
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-disk\-write\-back\fR
Don\[aq]t default to enabling write-back for disk images.
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-disk\-auto\-os9\fR
Don\[aq]t try to detect headerless OS-9 JVC disk images.
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-disk\-auto\-sd\fR
Don\[aq]t assume single density for 10 sec/track disks.
.H2 Hard disks:
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-hd\fIX\fB\fR \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR as the hard disk image for drive \fIX\fR (0–1).
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-sd\fR \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR as the SD card image (e.g. for mooh, nx32).
.H2 Keyboard:
.TP
\f(CB\-kbd\-layout\fR \fIlayout\fR
Host keyboard layout (\f(CB\-kbd\-layout help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-kbd\-lang\fR \fIlang\fR
Host keyboard language (\f(CB\-kbd\-lang help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-kbd\-bind\fR \fIhostkey\fR=\[lB]pre:\[rB]\fIemukey\fR
Map host key to emulated key. Prefixing emulated key name with \[aq]pre:\[aq] disables translation for the bind (the bind "preempts" translation). Host key names can be determined by running with \f(CB\-debug\-ui 1\fR, which will log keypresses.
.TP
\f(CB\-kbd\-translate\fR
Enable keyboard translation.
.TP
\f(CB\-type\fR \fIstring\fR
Intercept ROM calls to type \fIstring\fR into BASIC.
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-text\fR \fIfile\fR
Type \fIfile\fR into BASIC.
.H2 Joysticks:
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\-db\-file\fR \fIfile\fR
Load gamepad mappings from \fIfile\fR.
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\-right\fR \fIname\fR
Map right joystick.
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\-left\fR \fIname\fR
Map left joystick.
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\-virtual\fR \fIname\fR
Specify the \[aq]virtual\[aq] joystick to cycle \[lB]kjoy0\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\fR \fIname\fR
Configure named joystick (\f(CB\-joy help\fR for list).
.PP
The remaining options configure the currently selected joystick:
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\-desc\fR \fItext\fR
Joystick description.
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\-axis\fR \fIaxis\fR=\fIspec\fR
Configure joystick axis.
.TP
\f(CB\-joy\-button\fR \fIbtn\fR=\fIspec\fR
Configure joystick button.
.PP
Joystick \fIspec\fRs are of the form \[lB]\fImodule\fR:\[rB]\[lB]\fIarg\fR\[lB],\fIarg\fR\[rB]\[...]\[rB], from:
.P
.TS
tab(@);
l l lx.
\fBModule\fR@\fBAxis \fIarg\fRs\fR@T{
\fBButton \fIarg\fRs\fR
T}
.T&
_ _ _
l l lx.
physical@joystick-index,\[lB]-\[rB]axis-index@T{
joystick-index,button-index
T}
keyboard@key-name0,key-name1@T{
key-name
T}
mouse@screen-offset0,screen-offset1@T{
button-number
T}
.TE
.PP
For physical joysticks a \[aq]-\[aq] before the axis index inverts the axis. Axis 0 is the X-axis, and axis 1 the Y-axis. Buttons are numbered 0 or 1 (the second is only used when connected to a CoCo 3).
.H2 Printers:
.TP
\f(CB\-lp\-file\fR \fIfile\fR
Append printer output to \fIfile\fR.
.TP
\f(CB\-lp\-pipe\fR \fIcommand\fR
Pipe printer output to \fIcommand\fR.
.H2 Files:
.TP
\f(CB\-load\fR \fIfile\fR
Load or attach \fIfile\fR
.TP
\f(CB\-run\fR \fIfile\fR
Load or attach \fIfile\fR and attempt autorun
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-fd\fIX\fB\fR \fIfile\fR
Insert disk image \fIfile\fR into floppy drive \fIX\fR (0–3).
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-hd\fIX\fB\fR \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR as the hard disk image for drive \fIX\fR (0–1).
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-sd\fR \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR as the SD card image (e.g. for mooh, nx32).
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-tape\fR \fIfile\fR
Attach \fIfile\fR as tape image for reading.
.TP
\f(CB\-tape\-write\fR \fIfile\fR
Open \fIfile\fR for tape writing.
.TP
\f(CB\-load\-text\fR \fIfile\fR
Type \fIfile\fR into BASIC.
.H2 Firmware ROM images:
.TP
\f(CB\-rompath\fR \fIpath\fR
ROM search path (colon-separated list).
.TP
\f(CB\-romlist\fR \fIname\fR=\fIlist\fR
Define a ROM list.
.TP
\f(CB\-romlist\-print\fR
Print defined ROM lists.
.TP
\f(CB\-crclist\fR \fIname\fR=\fIlist\fR
Define a ROM CRC list.
.TP
\f(CB\-crclist\-print\fR
Print defined ROM CRC lists.
.TP
\f(CB\-force\-crc\-match\fR
Force per-architecture CRC matches.
.H2 User interface:
.TP
\f(CB\-ui\fR \fImodule\fR
User-interface module (\f(CB\-ui help\fR for list).
.H2 Video:
.TP
\f(CB\-fs\fR
Start emulator full-screen if possible.
.TP
\f(CB\-fskip\fR \fIframes\fR
Frameskip (default: 0).
.TP
\f(CB\-ccr\fR \fIrenderer\fR
Cross-colour renderer (\f(CBsimple\fR, \f(CB5bit\fR, \f(CBpartial\fR or \f(CBsimulated\fR).
.TP
\f(CB\-gl\-filter\fR \fIfilter\fR
OpenGL texture filter (\f(CBauto\fR, \f(CBnearest\fR or \f(CBlinear\fR).
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-vsync\fR
Start with vsync enabled.
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-pixel\-fmt\fR \fIformat\fR
Pixel format (\f(CB\-vo\-pixel\-fmt help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-geometry\fR \fIw\fRx\fIh\fR+\fIx\fR+\fIy\fR
Initial emulator geometry.
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-picture\fR \fIp\fR
Initial picture area (\f(CB\-vo\-picture help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-vo\-scale\-60hz\fR
Disable vertical scaling for 60Hz video.
.TP
\f(CB\-invert\-text\fR
Start with text mode inverted.
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-brightness\fR \fIn\fR
Set TV brightness (0–100) \[lB]50\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-contrast\fR \fIn\fR
Set TV contrast (0–100) \[lB]50\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-colour\fR \fIn\fR
Set TV colour saturation (0–100) \[lB]50\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-hue\fR \fIn\fR
Set TV hue control (-179 to +180) \[lB]0\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-vo\-monochrome\fR
Use a black-and-white display (disabled by default).
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-vo\-colour\-killer\fR
Disable colour killer (enabled by default).
.H2 Audio:
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\fR \fImodule\fR
Audio module (\f(CB\-ao help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-device\fR \fIstring\fR
Device to use for audio module.
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR
Set audio sample format (\f(CB\-ao\-format help\fR for list).
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-rate\fR \fIhz\fR
Set audio frame rate (if supported by module).
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-channels\fR \fIn\fR
Set number of audio channels, \f(CB1\fR or \f(CB2\fR.
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-fragments\fR \fIn\fR
Set number of audio fragments.
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-fragment\-ms\fR \fIms\fR
Set audio fragment size in ms (if supported).
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-fragment\-frames\fR \fIn\fR
Set audio fragment size in samples (if supported).
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-buffer\-ms\fR \fIms\fR
Set total audio buffer size in ms (if supported).
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-buffer\-frames\fR \fIn\fR
Set total audio buffer size in samples (if supported).
.TP
\f(CB\-ao\-gain\fR \fIdb\fR
Audio gain in dB relative to 0 dBFS \[lB]-3.0\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-volume\fR \fIvolume\fR
Older way to specify audio volume, linear (0–100).
.H2 Debugging:
.TP
\f(CB\-gdb\fR
Enable GDB target.
.TP
\f(CB\-gdb\-ip\fR \fIaddress\fR
Address of interface for GDB target \[lB]127.0.0.1\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-gdb\-port\fR \fIport\fR
Port for GDB target to listen on \[lB]65520\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-gdb\-pseudo\-regs\fR
Enable pseudo-registers (e.g. SAM, PIA) for GDB.
.TP
\f(CB\-gdb\-flags\-as\-struct\fR
Describe CPU flags as a struct to GDB.
.TP
\f(CB\-no\-ratelimit\fR
Run CPU as fast as possible.
.TP
\f(CB\-trace\fR
Start with trace mode on.
.TP
\f(CB\-trace\-timing\fR
Print timings in trace mode.
.TP
\f(CB\-debug\-fdc\fR \fIflags\fR
FDC debugging (see manual, or \f(CB\-1\fR for all).
.TP
\f(CB\-debug\-file\fR \fIflags\fR
File debugging (see manual, or \f(CB\-1\fR for all).
.TP
\f(CB\-debug\-gdb\fR \fIflags\fR
GDB target debugging (see manual, or \f(CB\-1\fR for all).
.TP
\f(CB\-debug\-ui\fR \fIflags\fR
UI debugging (see manual, or \f(CB\-1\fR for all).
.TP
\f(CB\-v, \-verbose\fR \fIlevel\fR
General debug verbosity (\f(CB0\fR to \f(CB3\fR) \[lB]1\[rB]
.TP
\f(CB\-q\fR, \f(CB\-quiet\fR
Equivalent to \f(CB\-verbose 0\fR.
.TP
\f(CB\-trap\fR \fIcondition\fR
Configure a trap to fire on \fIcondition\fR.
.PP
These options affect the configured trap:
.TP
\f(CB\-trap\-range\fR \fIm\fR-\fIn\fR
Perform trap\[aq]s action only on \fIm\fRth-\fIn\fRth trigger.
.TP
\f(CB\-trap\-snap\fR \fIfile\fR
Write snapshot at trap.
.TP
\f(CB\-trap\-timeout\fR \fIn\fR
Quit emulator \fIn\fR seconds after trap.
.TP
\f(CB\-trap\-trace\fR
Start trace mode at trap.
.TP
\f(CB\-trap\-trace\-n\fR \fIn\fR
Start trace mode at trap for \fIn\fR instructions.
.TP
\f(CB\-trap\-no\-trace\fR
Stop trace mode at trap.
.PP
Trap \fIcondition\fRs can be one of the following:
.P
.TS
tab(;);
l lx.
\fBCondition\fR;T{
\fBAction\fR
T}
.T&
_ _
l lx.
immediate (or \[aq]-\[aq]);T{
trigger immediately
T}
pc=\fIaddr\fR;T{
trigger at CPU Program Counter value
T}
read=\fIa\fR\[lB]-\fIb\fR\[rB];T{
trigger on read from address range
T}
write=\fIa\fR\[lB]-\fIb\fR\[rB];T{
trigger on write to address range
T}
access=\fIa\fR\[lB]-\fIb\fR\[rB];T{
trigger on either read or write
T}
tape-motor-off;T{
trigger when tape motor switches off
T}
.TE
.PP
Older options remain that can be implemented using traps:
.TP
\f(CB\-timeout\fR \fIs\fR
Run for \fIs\fR seconds then quit.
.TP
\f(CB\-timeout\-motoroff\fR \fIs\fR
Quit \fIs\fR seconds after tape motor switches off.
.TP
\f(CB\-snap\-motoroff\fR \fIfile\fR
Write a snapshot each time tape motor switches off.
.H2 Other options:
.TP
\f(CB\-config\-print\fR
Print configuration to standard out, omitting (most) default options.
.TP
\f(CB\-config\-print\-all\fR
Print configuration to standard out, including defaults.
.TP
\f(CB\-config\-auto\-save\fR
Write configuration to \fI$HOME/.xroar/xroar.conf\fR on exit.
.TP
\f(CB\-h\fR, \f(CB\-\-help\fR
Display help and exit.
.TP
\f(CB\-V\fR, \f(CB\-\-version\fR
Output version information and exit.
.H1 KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.P
.TS
tab(;);
l lx.
\fBShortcut\fR;T{
\fBAction\fR
T}
.T&
_ _
l lx.
CTRL+\[lB]1–4\[rB];T{
Insert disk into drive 1–4.
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+\[lB]1–4\[rB];T{
Create new disk in drive 1–4.
T}
CTRL+\[lB]5–8\[rB];T{
Toggle write enable on disk in drive 1–4.
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+\[lB]5–8\[rB];T{
Toggle write back on disk in drive 1–4.
T}
CTRL+A;T{
Cycle through cross-colour modes (and RGB on CoCo 3).
T}
CTRL+D;T{
Open disk control tool (GTK+ & Windows only).
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+D;T{
Flush disk images.
T}
CTRL+E;T{
Toggle cartridge on/off - reset to take effect.
T}
CTRL+F;T{
Toggle full screen mode.
T}
or F11;T{

T}
CTRL+SHIFT+H;T{
Halt the CPU (not on the MC-10).
T}
or PAUSE;T{

T}
CTRL+SHIFT+I;T{
Toggle text mode inverse video.
T}
CTRL+J;T{
Cycle through joystick emulation modes (None, Right, Left).
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+J;T{
Swap left and right joysticks.
T}
CTRL+K;T{
Toggle Dragon/CoCo keyboard layout (not on the MC-10).
T}
CTRL+L;T{
Load a file.
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+L;T{
Load and attempt to autorun a file.
T}
CTRL+M;T{
Toggle menubar.
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+P;T{
Flush printer output.
T}
CTRL+Q;T{
Quit emulator.
T}
CTRL+R;T{
Soft reset emulated machine.
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+R;T{
Hard reset emulated machine.
T}
CTRL+S;T{
Save a snapshot.
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+S;T{
Write screenshot as PNG.
T}
CTRL+T;T{
Open the tape control tool (GTK+ & Windows only).
T}
CTRL+V;T{
Toggle trace mode.
T}
CTRL+SHIFT+V;T{
Open TV controls window (GTK+ & Windows only).
T}
CTRL+W;T{
Attach a virtual cassette file for writing.
T}
CTRL+Z;T{
Enable keyboard translation mode.
T}
CTRL+-;T{
Zoom out (smaller emulated display).
T}
CTRL++;T{
Zoom in (larger emulated display).
T}
CTRL+<;T{
Zoom out picture (see more border).
T}
CTRL+>;T{
Zoom in picture area (see less border).
T}
F12;T{
Run at maximum speed while held.
T}
SHIFT+F12;T{
Maximum speed toggle.
T}
.TE
